# Task 152-003 Execution Plan — CLI Smoke Part 1

## Approach
READ-ONLY audit sprint. No code changes. Run `node dist/cli/entry.js <cmd>` for 15 core lifecycle commands, capture stdout/stderr/exit code, assess PASS/FAIL/REGRESSION/MISSING.

## Commands (15)
1. init --help (+ dry-run if supported)
2. doctor
3. analyze-project --help
4. plan --help (+ dry-run)
5. start --help (+ --dry-run)
6. status --help + --json
7. review --help
8. retro --help
9. history
10. cleanup --help (NO actual run — destructive)
11. help
12. config read
13. config set --help
14. docs list
15. explain --help

## Safety
- NEVER run `cleanup` without `--help` or `--dry-run`
- NEVER run `kill` at all
- NEVER run `start` without --dry-run

## Output
Single report file: docs/audits/sprint-152/T-152-003-cli-core-lifecycle.md
Format: per-command section with verdict + evidence snippets.
